{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JEiyYh2AcUvbhebec2eThP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Shared primary-reference packet\n2\t\n3\tIdentical in both arms. This packet supplies library/format semantics, not finding\n4\tlocations or an answer key. Recorded 2026-10-23. Model web lookup is unavailable.\n5\t\n6\t- Express 4 error handling: https://expressjs.com/en/4x/guide/error-handling/\n7\t  Official framework documentation, retrieved 2026-10-23. Rejected async-handler\n8\t  promises need explicit forwarding to the framework error path.\n9\t- Node 20 runtime options: https://nodejs.org/download/release/latest-v20.x/docs/api/cli.html#--unhandled-rejectionsmode\n10\t  Official runtime documentation, retrieved 2026-10-23. The default unhandled\n11\t  rejection mode raises an uncaught exception when no relevant hook is installed.\n12\t- Desktop manifest 0.1: https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/mcpb/blob/v0.1.0/MANIFEST.md#user-configuration\n13\t  Versioned format specification. The sensitive string option requests masked\n14\t  input and secure storage; its default is false. Installed-host behavior still\n15\t  needs evidence.\n16\t- MCP security guidance: https://modelcontextprotocol.io/docs/2026-07-28/tutorials/security/security_best_practices\n17\t  Protocol-project guidance, bundled review date 2026-10-22. Scope credential,\n18\t  process and transport boundaries to the component actually supplied.\n19\t- TypeScript SDK redirect advisory: https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk/security/advisories/GHSA-6prh-2h8m-c8cw\n20\t  Maintainer advisory, published 2026-10-02, checked 2026-10-23. SDK HTTP clients\n21\t  before 1.32.0 can forward custom headers and request bodies across redirects.\n22\t  Check package, version and use of the affected client; an unrelated component\n23\t  is not vulnerable merely because it participates in MCP.\n24\t- OWASP Logging: https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Log